WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.182
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.182 --> 00:00:12.790
Traits, part two: what a trait actually does to a character.

5
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.562
Open Mechanics, then Traits, then Traits.

6
00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:22.236
Here's every trait, and I've added a new act, Fire Eater.

7
00:00:22.236 --> 00:00:23.384
Let's open it.

8
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:27.021
The description is what players read when they pick it,

9
00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:31.020
and trait narrative effects are what the narrator works from in play.

10
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.685
Usually they're the same paragraph, like ours.

11
00:00:33.685 --> 00:00:37.742
Split them when the narrator needs something the player shouldn't see.

12
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.798
Unlocked by and excluded by are the gates.

13
00:00:40.798 --> 00:00:45.872
Fire Eater is unlocked by Born on the Road, so only road-born players ever see it.

14
00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:51.749
In the creator they only look at picks from earlier pages, and they can name a story start too.

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.962
Requirements only matter for level-up trait picks.

16
00:00:55.962 --> 00:00:57.842
The creator ignores them.

17
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.076
Skills and attributes add straight onto the character's own.

18
00:01:02.076 --> 00:01:07.236
Fire Eater raises constitution and charisma and gives a head start in performance,

19
00:01:07.236 --> 00:01:11.264
and a skill the character didn't have gets added to their sheet.

20
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.524
Abilities on a trait are handed over directly, skipping the move's own requirements.

21
00:01:16.524 --> 00:01:21.406
Starting items come with it at creation or a level-up pick, but never from a trigger.

22
00:01:21.406 --> 00:01:23.531
Our barker starts with the ring coat.

23
00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:25.167
And resistances.

24
00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:28.092
Fire Eater takes half damage from fire.

25
00:01:28.092 --> 00:01:34.241
A vulnerability takes one and a half times the damage, and an immunity takes none.

26
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:39.463
Remember the premades from episode ten, with no traits yet?

27
00:01:39.463 --> 00:01:42.514
Now Nell's got hers: she ran off with the show,

28
00:01:42.514 --> 00:01:45.954
so she's Ran Away to Join, and she's a knife thrower.

29
00:01:45.954 --> 00:01:48.811
Jack got Ran Away to Join and Escape Artist.

30
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.824
One warning. If you change a trait after people have started playing,

31
00:01:54.824 --> 00:01:57.169
only new characters get the change.

32
00:01:57.169 --> 00:02:00.185
Characters already made keep the old version.

33
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.601
That's traits.

34
00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:05.603
Our full set is linked in the description.

35
00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:10.679
Next time, success levels: how a roll turns into what actually happens.

36
00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:15.081
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

